//   hull of points, and a polyline sampled from a 2-D Bezier curve; and the
//   functions behind the last two, 'convexHull' and 'sampleCurve' (any of
//   geomath's Bezier curves, 2-D or 3-D, as a List of points).
// - Path, a 3-D polyline sampled from Bezier curves or given as points, and
//   the frames along it: rotation-minimizing frames, by the double-reflection
//   method; 'curveFrames', the same as sdf's CurveFrames, which with
//   'distances' are what an sdf.PathCurve views.
// - Profile to solid: 'extrude' (along a direction), 'lathe' (revolved about
//   an axis) and 'sweep' (along a path, with twist and taper; 'sweepScaled'
//   with the scale any function of arc length), each making a
//   mesh.PolyMesh of quads, with a corner "uv" channel and the vertex
//   channels "along" and "around" (see below).
// - Lofts and bridges: 'loft' (a surface through profiles placed in given
//   frames) and 'loftAlong' (placed along a path, following it), the
//   profiles of any counts and shapes put on common columns and started so
//   the band does not twist, joined linearly or by a Catmull-Rom spline, with
//   rings between and optional caps, writing "uv", "along" and "around" as
//   the other generators do; 'bridgeLoops' (a band of faces joining boundary
//   loops of a mesh in pairs, as Blender's Bridge Edge Loops, with cuts and a
//   smoothness that leaves each loop along its surface) and 'boundaryLoop'.
// - Deformers, which move a PolyMesh's vertices and leave its topology and
//   channels as they were: 'bend', 'twist' and 'taper' (Barr's global
//   deformations, as Blender's Simple Deform modifier offers them),
//   'curveDeform' (a mesh laid along a path, as Blender's Curve modifier),
//   and 'displaceAlongNormal' (each vertex along its normal by a stored
//   channel's value times an amount, as Blender's Displace modifier).
//   Each has a form fed by a function, written as a closure at the call:
//   'deform' (every vertex to f(p), as Blender's Set Position),
//   'deformAlong' (every vertex offset by f(u), u its fraction along an
//   axis), 'taper' and 'twist' given a function in place of the number (the
//   scale or the turn about an axis as a function of u), and
//   'displaceAlongNormal' given a function in place of the channel (the
//   amount a function of the vertex's index, which reads its channels
//   through the mesh).
// - Lattice (free-form deformation): 'Lattice', a box spanned by three axes
//   and a grid of l x m x n control points over it, read, set and moved one
//   by one, and 'latticeDeform', each vertex moved by the control points'
//   moves weighted at its place in the box, by Bernstein polynomials
//   (Sederberg and Parry's FFD), trilinearly, or by a clamped uniform cubic
//   B-spline ('latticeWeights' gives the weights), as Blender's Lattice
//   modifier; the topology and every channel are kept.
// - Copies and merging: 'mirror' (the mesh and its reflection in a plane,
