// A bend (Blender's Simple Deform, Bend; Barr's bend): the mesh's span along
// 'along' is curled through 'angle' about 'axis' (made perpendicular to
// along), turning along towards c = axis x along, as a right-handed turn
// about the axis does. With the span's length S, the bend's radius is
// R = S / angle, and its centre line runs parallel to the axis through
// origin + c R. A vertex at t along, c' across towards c and w along the
// axis, with T = t clamped to the span and theta = T / R, goes to
//     origin + along ((R - c') sin theta + (t - T) cos theta)
//            + c (R - (R - c') cos theta + (t - T) sin theta) + axis w:
// within the span, onto the arc of radius R - c' about the centre line at
// angle theta from the origin, so a straight line along the span through the
// origin becomes an arc of radius R, turning through 'angle', whose length
// is unchanged; outside the span, carried on straight along the tangent at
// the span's end. A negative angle bends towards -c.
pub extern fn bend(m: &PolyMesh, angle: f32, axis: Vec3, along: Vec3, origin: Vec3) PolyMesh;
