// ======== Multiresolution: subdivision levels that keep their detail ========
//
// As Blender's Multiresolution modifier and ZBrush's subdivision levels: a
// base mesh (level 0) and n levels of Catmull-Clark subdivision above it,
// each level's detail kept as displacements from the level below, so a
// sculpt at a high level and a reshape of the base are both kept. A Multires
// holds, for each level, the evaluated mesh (its topology, channels and
// positions) and, for each level above the base, its detail.
//
// What a level is made of. Level k's reference surface is the subdivision of
// level k-1's positions (the smooth surface the level below promises); a
// vertex of level k is its reference point plus its detail:
//     P_k[v] = R_k[v] + t[v] c[v].x + b[v] c[v].y + n[v] c[v].z
// where R_k is 'refPositions' of level k-1, (t, b, n) is a frame at the
// reference point and c the stored detail, three numbers. The frame is
// worked out on the reference surface alone (n the vertex's normal there,
// angle-weighted over its faces; t the direction of its first edge, with n's
// part taken out; b = n x t), so it depends on the level below and nothing
// else, and detail rides along: reshape or pose a lower level and every
// level above is rebuilt from its own detail in the new frames, a bump on a
// bent arm still standing out from the new arm. (Blender stores each level's
// displacement in the tangent space of the subdivided surface and so does
// this; the frame here is the subdivided level's normal, not the limit
// surface's, which the next level's reference converges to.)
//
// Numbering is subdivide's: level k's vertices 0 to V-1, those of level
// k-1, are the same points, so a vertex of the base is a vertex of every
// level, then the edge points, then the face points. A level's mesh is the
// subdivision of the level below with positions as above, and every channel
// is carried by subdivision's rules (a crease wears down a level a time).
//
// Operations (each named for what Blender or ZBrush calls it):
// - 'Multires.fromMesh': a base with no levels yet; 'addLevel' (Blender's
//   Subdivide, ZBrush's Divide): one more level, detail zero, so the surface
//   is the smooth subdivision;
// - 'fromDense' (ZBrush's Reconstruct Subdiv, Blender's Rebuild Subdivisions):
//   a dense mesh whose topology is the subdivision of a simpler one, taken
//   back to a base and levels, the base and each lower level the least
//   squares fit of the level above (see multiresrebuild.cone); the top level
//   is the dense mesh itself, exactly;
// - 'evaluate' (any level's mesh), 'apply' (the top level as a plain
//   PolyMesh, Blender's Apply);
// - 'editLevel': a level given new positions; the detail below it is kept
//   and the detail at it is what the new positions leave, so an edit at a
//   high level is stored as detail, and an edit at a low level (the base
//   included, 'setBase') moves every level above it, smoothly, by their
//   detail in the new frames;
// - 'deleteHigher' (Blender's Delete Higher, ZBrush's Del Higher), 'deleteLower'
//   (ZBrush's Del Lower: a level becomes the base, the levels above are
//   kept exactly as they were); 'bakeDown' (as Blender's Apply Base: each
//   lower level takes the shape of the top, its vertices being the top's, and
//   the detail is rewritten so that no level above changes);
// - 'displacement': the offset between two levels as vertex channels on the
//   upper level's mesh, for a later normal-map or displacement-map baker;
// - storage: 'levelBytes', 'packLevel', 'unpackLevel' and 'quantize': a
//   level's detail as float32, or as signed integers of 8 or 16 bits with one
//   scale per component, the candidate format for sending sculpted detail
//   (see multresstore.cone).
//
// Sharp creases, boundaries and face-varying data follow 'subdivide' with the
// boundary and face-varying rules the Multires was made with (subdivide's
// defaults for 'fromMesh').

pub struct Multires {
  pub levels: List[PolyMesh];      // levels[k]: level k as evaluated; levels[0] is the base
  pub detail: List[List[Vec3]];    // detail[k-1]: level k's, per vertex, (t, b, n) coefficients
  pub boundary: u32;
  pub fvar: u32;

  // A base and no levels above it, with subdivide's defaults
  pub extern fn fromMesh(base: &PolyMesh) Multires;
