// ======== Ribs that melt: a rib phase field, and a growing margin ========
//
// Two ways to fill a vertex channel with ribs across a swept, lathed or
// extruded mesh, read from its "along" (0 at the start, 1 at the end) and
// "around" (0 to 1 round the outline) channels. Each writes a channel of
// crest height about 1 (0 between ribs); the caller scales it (by the local
// radius, say) and moves the surface with displaceAlongNormal.
//
// THE PHASE FIELD (ribField). Ribs are the crests of a phase: rib k runs
// where the phase is k + 1/2, and the troughs where it is a whole number.
// The height is
//
//   A(p) * h(k) * (sin^2(pi phase))^sharpness,   k = floor(phase),
//
// and the phase is frequency * along, plus four terms, each off at its
// default:
// - warp: warp * fbm3(p * warpScale), p the vertex's position, so the ribs
//   wander and tilt (a warp of 1 moves a rib by up to about a rib);
// - the envelope A: smoothstep of a slow fbm3(p * coverScale) against a
//   threshold set by 'cover', so ribs fade out in patches ('cover' 1 or more:
//   A = 1 everywhere, no noise is asked);
// - each rib's own height h(k) = 1 + spread * u, and with chance 'absent' no
//   rib at all, u and the chance hashed from (seed, k): a rib keeps its
//   number however it wanders, so the whole rib is tall or missing;
// - 'defects' pairs of phase vortices: one rib forks in a Y and the two
//   rejoin a little further round (a dislocation pair, as in fingerprints
//   and stripe patterns). A vortex at (s0, t0) adds arg(1 - e^-z) / 2 pi,
//   z = (along - s0) aspect + i (theta - t0), theta = 2 pi around: near the
//   vortex that is arg z, one turn of phase round it, and it repeats every
//   turn of theta, so it is seamless round the mesh. The pair's two are
//   taken together as arg(f1 conj f2), which sends the jump of a whole rib
//   only along a short cut between them; above both the phase is unchanged,
//   below both shifted by a constant. 'defectAspect' converts along to the
//   same scale as theta: a horn of length L and radius r wants L / r, so a
//   vortex is round on the surface.
// Every random number is a hash of (seed, a term's index, a rib's number or
// a pair's number), never a stream; noise is noise.fbm3, 3 octaves.
//
// THE MARGIN RING (marginRing). A horn or shell grows at its rim; its ribs
// are what the rim was doing when each ring was laid down (Meinhardt, The
// Algorithmic Beauty of Sea Shells; Fowler, Meinhardt and Prusinkiewicz
// 1992). Here the rim is a ring of 'cells' cells running the Brusselator, an
// oscillating reaction-diffusion (Prigogine and Lefever 1968):
//
//   a' = A_i - (B + 1) a + a^2 b + Da (a[i-1] + a[i+1] - 2 a)
//   b' = B a - a^2 b              + Db (b[i-1] + b[i+1] - 2 b)
//
// which, for B > 1 + A^2, pulses: each pulse of a is one rib round the rim.
// 'unevenness' makes each cell's A_i differ, by noise.gradient3 round the
// ring that drifts slowly with growth, so cells run at different rates, and
// ribs tilt, fork and end where the ring slips a beat. Measured: diffusion
// does not hold even an even ring in step at the plain settings (A 1, B 3,
// both diffusions 0.4): a start difference of 0.2% between cells grows to
// the full swing within about six periods (Cone and a numpy run of the same
// equations agree), so the ribs fall into waves round the ring even with no
// unevenness; less diffusion breaks them up more. The run lasts 'frequency' periods of one
// cell's pulse (measured first, from one cell alone), so 'frequency' ribs
// span along 0 to 1. A vertex's height is a, between the lone cell's least
// and greatest, at its along (in time) and its around (on the ring), both
// interpolated linearly. Explicit Euler, 400 steps a period.

pub struct RibField {
  pub frequency: f32;     // ribs from along 0 to along 1
  pub sharpness: f32;     // the crest's exponent: 1 a plain sine squared, larger narrower
  pub warp: f32;          // the phase's warp, in ribs; 0 none
  pub warpScale: f32;     // the warp noise's cells per unit of position
  pub cover: f32;         // the share of the surface ribbed, roughly; 1 or more: all
  pub coverScale: f32;    // the envelope noise's cells per unit of position
  pub spread: f32;        // each rib's height 1 + spread * u, u in [-1, 1); 0 all alike
  pub absent: f32;        // each rib's chance of being missing; 0 none
  pub defects: u32;       // pairs of phase vortices; 0 none
  pub defectAspect: f32;  // along's scale against theta's for the vortices
  pub seed: u32;

  // Regular ribs: 'frequency' of them, sharpness 3, and no other term
  pub extern fn plain(frequency: f32, seed: u32) RibField;
//#line 79 "ribs.cone"
}

